            <ArticleTitle>Navifocus WR is the promising intravascular ultrasound for navigating the guidewire into true lumen during the coronary intervention for chronic total occlusion.</ArticleTitle>
            <Pagination>
                <MedlinePgn>181-6</MedlinePgn>
            </Pagination>
            <ELocationID EIdType="doi" ValidYN="Y">10.1007/s12928-013-0212-x</ELocationID>
            <Abstract>
                <AbstractText>We describe an initial clinical chronic total occlusion (CTO) case in which CTO-specific intravascular ultrasound (IVUS): Navifocus WR was useful for navigating the second guidewire into the true lumen under the IVUS observation from the subintimal space.</AbstractText>
            </Abstract>
